{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/smoke-remote.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"76213ba062bf2f51a9dcb6b14732a6b6df46d9fd2be975b05fdd14f2720faa03","body":{"detail":"wrangler's docs say remote: true on an artifacts binding uses the remote service in local dev; whether that holds with --local and wrangler 4.149.0 is unverified. Locally the binding answers 'Binding ARTIFACTS needs to be run remotely'. If it works it gives a probe of the real service without a deploy.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":585},"end":{"line":590},"content_hash":"765d646f83c57f6bfd8c11ce9c56e0694989cbb0bd8310228dc0a9cf9e38cdfc"},"summary":"--remote-artifacts (the local Worker on the account's real Artifacts through the binding's remote: true) has not run: it needs a login, and harness.mjs starts wrangler dev with --local","supersedes":"4854d787a4833aea89d19dd5e75c7a3143dfe78c2612be02169652b1731c3277","tags":["deploy","artifacts","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.853436Z","id":"68b4866befebe81db5fb79f0449259300706b9edbb38a54894bab2a3f596f838","body":{"detail":"The owner is told to delete the record once set up; CLAX_TOKEN there stays valid until rotated (deploy.mjs --rotate-secrets). An alternative is printing them only and having smoke-remote.mjs take them from the environment, at the cost of the one-command smoke.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":314},"end":{"line":319},"content_hash":"414d576933fd9210f222e847e6f372f2975ebe1fa1583e8a77b8eedd6675d13d"},"summary":"deploy.mjs keeps the generated SETUP_SECRET and CLAX_TOKEN in plain text in crates/clax-worker/.deploy/<public host>.json (0600, git-ignored) so smoke-remote.mjs can use them","supersedes":"bef595b64d34d5bcbde5cd7bd6be41ded484d86fee253b6418123a0514d03583","tags":["deploy","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/Cargo.lock","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:18:40.364921Z","id":"282372641c9aaf8a5802d2848adfba69d307843d292176dd78019231a61a29ff","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-worker is its own Cargo workspace with its own lockfile (crates/clax-worker/Cargo.toml), and 20e1ed98c3fc added roxmltree 0.20 to crates/clax-core/Cargo.toml and the root Cargo.lock only: the Worker lock's clax-core entry lists no roxmltree and the file has no roxmltree package. A --locked build of the Worker fails, and a build without it (worker-build, crates/clax-worker/build.sh) rewrites the lock, leaving a dirty tree. 2894d3f96 fixed the same kind of drift for dirs. roxmltree 0.20 itself suits wasm32: no dependencies, #![no_std] with an std feature, #![forbid(unsafe_code)], MIT OR Apache-2.0.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":279},"end":{"line":308},"content_hash":"302203f4a7f954b6abf500cbf5502f78b50dbc66192ffdec0786279f91bdda3b"},"suggested_fix":"Add roxmltree 0.20.0 to crates/clax-worker/Cargo.lock (its checksum is in the root Cargo.lock) and to clax-core's dependency list there.","summary":"The Worker's own Cargo.lock was not updated for clax-core's new roxmltree dependency","tags":["review","icon","wasm","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/Cargo.lock","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:35:11.460931Z","id":"4b2b5013b3ec188653a69446c5a24a583e211d66465702b05a11fdf95fe15662","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"roxmltree 0.20.0 is locked and listed under clax-core. cargo metadata --locked --offline --manifest-path crates/clax-worker/Cargo.toml exited 101 ('cannot update the lock file ... because --locked was passed') before and 0 after; no target/ was made. No script in the repository checks the Worker lock's completeness (scripts/check-version.sh checks only Clax crates' versions).","supersedes":"282372641c9aaf8a5802d2848adfba69d307843d292176dd78019231a61a29ff","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T20:43:54.351330Z","id":"348cfd981b134f9ae9e35fd3aa6991c70c25b7642b9d29ea094f8baaabee2db9","body":{"detail":"Only //crates/clax-worker:rustfmt is Bazel's; scripts/worker-checks.sh runs the Worker's tests and clippy with Cargo in CI's worker job. crates/clax-worker/Cargo.lock resolves the Clax crates' dependencies apart from the root's (on 2026-10-20 35 shared crates differ, e.g. tokio 1.53.2 vs 1.53.1, serde_json 1.0.154 vs 1.0.151, and 9 crates such as worker, worker-sys and strum are in it alone), so the Worker cannot link the root's //crates/* libraries built from @crates. A second crate_universe repo from the Worker's lockfile does not cover the Clax crates it uses by path: cargo-bazel copies such a path crate into an external repository (local_crate_mirror), where include_str! of files outside the crate (clax-core's ../../../web/extension/manifest.json, clax-server's web/contract/*.d.ts, clax-testkit's ../../clax-server/src/router.rs) does not resolve, and its hub aliases only the workspace members' direct dependencies, so first-party copies of those crates cannot name their third-party dependencies. Either way the Clax crates would be compiled a second time against other dependency versions, growing CI's 6 GB disk cache.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":35},"content_hash":"a358426273ce7f971a79807f72458ef04df84e1eb64cf4174cee11cb52160f7c"},"summary":"Build and test crates/clax-worker and its VFS under Bazel (cargo_package, clippy aspect, rust_test), not only its format check","tags":["build","ci","revisit:crates/clax-worker joins the root Cargo workspace or shares its Cargo.lock, or rules_rust's crate_universe resolves path dependencies outside the workspace with their compile data","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/Cargo.lock","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T10:42:13.941778Z","id":"2bb376a7369c5ce5d10c333cb9484621619aa68c70bec5d913e20bf60fed719e","body":{"detail":"clax-server depends on qrcode 0.14 (crates/clax-server/Cargo.toml, Cargo.toml workspace dependencies), and the workspace Cargo.lock has it, but the Worker's own lockfile was not updated. Running just worker-test adds qrcode 0.14.1 to the clax-server dependencies and a [[package]] entry, leaving the checkout dirty.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":436},"end":{"line":470},"content_hash":"18ba4a79ad2d879595f2009ec192db670f0e156e278b0c723ed417e9db0fbe74"},"suggested_fix":"Run the Worker's build once (just worker-test) and commit the updated crates/clax-worker/Cargo.lock.","summary":"crates/clax-worker/Cargo.lock does not list qrcode, so the next Worker build rewrites it","tags":["app-push","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/Cargo.lock","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T10:46:50.293448Z","id":"7b5b3c49665d8ef920f65d7a5fcbe5d3397e090642e5aa99995a772b650dc855","body":{"detail":"clax-server depends on qrcode 0.14 (crates/clax-server/Cargo.toml, Cargo.toml workspace dependencies), and the workspace Cargo.lock has it, but the Worker's own lockfile was not updated. Running just worker-test adds qrcode 0.14.1 to the clax-server dependencies and a [[package]] entry, leaving the checkout dirty.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":436},"end":{"line":469},"content_hash":"7ec6d4b3ab978bb73d23396d8a9e3c1ee77f2aa3a8bcbfd0d83f54a6760d5ee0"},"suggested_fix":"Run the Worker's build once (just worker-test) and commit the updated crates/clax-worker/Cargo.lock.","summary":"crates/clax-worker/Cargo.lock does not list qrcode, so the next Worker build rewrites it","supersedes":"2bb376a7369c5ce5d10c333cb9484621619aa68c70bec5d913e20bf60fed719e","tags":["app-push","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/Cargo.lock","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T11:42:19.044681Z","id":"143b8d1737a05a3d5c6add4ed60ddc83c33cd4f72502964e529c3a610129b22d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e3dc56eff","summary":"crates/clax-worker/Cargo.lock now lists qrcode 0.14.1 under clax-server. just worker-test exited 0 (cargo test, clippy and test-wasm.mjs all ok) and left git status clean after the commit.","supersedes":"7b5b3c49665d8ef920f65d7a5fcbe5d3397e090642e5aa99995a772b650dc855","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/test-bot.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:17:22.421002Z","id":"8af08fe94af92dbc3abda2cb5071068933c7981737264693959eb1560aca0df9","body":{"detail":"ServerHost::write, publish and reply return not_yet (crates/clax-server/src/bot.rs). The script catches the error and the test prints a note; once the host writes, the same check asserts version 2 and a reply comment.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":323},"end":{"line":325},"content_hash":"3b64a2fb750d997b493bf64ffdb09bc7ebef7d1a9a87bf5c28d240894f99e4e5"},"summary":"test-bot.mjs checks the script's publish and reply only once clax_server::bot::ServerHost writes: it answers unavailable now, so a run's publish and thread reply have not run on the Worker","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:17:22.421638Z","id":"28d3ddb69b2ab8505360c7ea4882038615cec8a50c3bd3ca061def2131386dc2","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"68b4866befebe81db5fb79f0449259300706b9edbb38a54894bab2a3f596f838","summary":"The record now also keeps CLAX_KEK (kek), ClaxBot's key-encryption key, in the same 0600 file: it is the only copy outside the Worker's secrets, and losing both loses every stored model key. deploy.mjs re-uploads the record's kek to a Worker that has none (kekPlan) and never rotates it.","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:18:19.734121Z","id":"ef20c1430e47689279bf7bc60d52dc32cc806bfd62a89382b7fecb01b16060cf","body":{"detail":"Only the logged-out --dry-run ran (no account was available): node deploy.mjs --dry-run --zone example.com passes and ends at wrangler deploy --dry-run (11.36 MiB, 4.36 MiB gzipped). Each logged-in step throws with wrangler's last error line and the command it ran, so a wrong pattern shows as a failed step rather than silently. If namespaces list answers a shape jsonIn does not parse, the namespace is taken as missing and a probe repository is created and deleted, which is harmless.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":168},"end":{"line":238},"content_hash":"b56127513f46b546e759ff598045a8c339be77ca93970ddebc103f6ecf534fe1"},"summary":"deploy.mjs's logged-in paths have not run: the whoami --json accounts shape, the 'already exists' patterns for r2 bucket create and queues create, artifacts namespaces list --json's shape, secret list --format json, and the account-scoped deploy with --secrets-file","supersedes":"61c8252ad530041c277dd059809fb9481703393efcc1eced47a4d98523f42ed2","tags":["deploy","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:18:19.757541Z","id":"47c3324f0ca30c3624c5a4c17f6eb597d51aeceaf9c7001b01f95e3f558cfb8a","body":{"detail":"The owner is told to delete the record once set up; CLAX_TOKEN there stays valid until rotated (deploy.mjs --rotate-secrets). An alternative is printing them only and having smoke-remote.mjs take them from the environment, at the cost of the one-command smoke.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":359},"end":{"line":363},"content_hash":"3f792a4841158150d836d343a2870bf4d63b9230c6b3a056b523f45beb8e9736"},"summary":"deploy.mjs keeps the generated SETUP_SECRET and CLAX_TOKEN in plain text in crates/clax-worker/.deploy/<public host>.json (0600, git-ignored) so smoke-remote.mjs can use them","supersedes":"68b4866befebe81db5fb79f0449259300706b9edbb38a54894bab2a3f596f838","tags":["deploy","security","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:15:16.321482Z","id":"6c3a6172414d9f9f5c2de1eff485fbc596bf1b650d0f0841091a29ba1434b285","body":{"detail":"The owner is told to delete the record once set up; CLAX_TOKEN there stays valid until rotated (deploy.mjs --rotate-secrets). An alternative is printing them only and having smoke-remote.mjs take them from the environment, at the cost of the one-command smoke.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":394},"end":{"line":398},"content_hash":"3f792a4841158150d836d343a2870bf4d63b9230c6b3a056b523f45beb8e9736"},"summary":"deploy.mjs keeps the generated SETUP_SECRET and CLAX_TOKEN in plain text in crates/clax-worker/.deploy/<public host>.json (0600, git-ignored) so smoke-remote.mjs can use them","supersedes":"47c3324f0ca30c3624c5a4c17f6eb597d51aeceaf9c7001b01f95e3f558cfb8a","tags":["deploy","security","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/test-bot.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:15:16.455516Z","id":"a248e2712f29c0cd33c13166341305b5ed4b9cbcb5bfb84e6acc6b22e9a30460","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:88645653","summary":"Fixed: ServerHost writes, and test-bot.mjs asserts the script publishes version 2 and replies once on the Worker, once each across the restart (node test-bot.mjs --no-build: 41 checks ok, three runs)","supersedes":"8af08fe94af92dbc3abda2cb5071068933c7981737264693959eb1560aca0df9","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:57:57.599175Z","id":"b5337d60198aaedf61e6c4884c50d897729ef7e27b3ee45d65aef2d0f8715a05","body":{"detail":"The owner is told to delete the record once set up; CLAX_TOKEN there stays valid until rotated (deploy.mjs --rotate-secrets). An alternative is printing them only and having smoke-remote.mjs take them from the environment, at the cost of the one-command smoke.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":401},"end":{"line":405},"content_hash":"3f792a4841158150d836d343a2870bf4d63b9230c6b3a056b523f45beb8e9736"},"summary":"deploy.mjs keeps the generated SETUP_SECRET and CLAX_TOKEN in plain text in crates/clax-worker/.deploy/<public host>.json (0600, git-ignored) so smoke-remote.mjs can use them","supersedes":"6c3a6172414d9f9f5c2de1eff485fbc596bf1b650d0f0841091a29ba1434b285","tags":["deploy","security","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:57:57.864038Z","id":"79115d20b0d6d78bb0b08bc5777657eb5448ab91a58eaed51a906fd7e81ffeb0","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"b5337d60198aaedf61e6c4884c50d897729ef7e27b3ee45d65aef2d0f8715a05","summary":"Since 59aca7bd and 904a6c2a CLAX_KEK is no longer kept in this record: deploy.mjs writes it to its own file, <host>.kek beside the record (0600), before the deploy, and moves a kek an old record held there; the record can be deleted once set up without losing the key.","tags":["session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/Cargo.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:50:56.264687Z","id":"4d7886934936f4b856641f9d67fd21578b7e0e09fc66ff1245d28a61fe033956","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-worker is its own workspace and uses clax-core, clax-rt and clax-server by path; its Cargo.lock was extended from the spike's, not seeded from the root Cargo.lock. A dependency the root pins (axum 0.8.9, rusqlite 0.40.2 agree today) can drift. Joining the root workspace would share one lockfile but pull workers-rs into every native build.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":25},"end":{"line":35},"content_hash":"c16d1c5374aac148adc8a5c3a92f7090bef7dea4c8289b36e3c487a974f7d454"},"summary":"The Worker's lockfile resolves the Clax crates' dependencies apart from the root's, so the Worker may build them at other versions than the daemon","supersedes":"af73cb2ed383f881021b778eb2194604afc102070e02a2aec2299aed7bb0c6b6","tags":["session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/smoke-remote.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T17:06:35.382925Z","id":"5a5d333772b5f07e87afa568f2bf65efe627fdb02ab52a74272b14b11c11baa3","body":{"detail":"When setup is closed and no --session is given, the owner step (OWNER) sets c.as = \"token\": the 'agent token' step skips, because POST /api/hosted/agent-tokens is browser_only (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs mint_token refuses any request with Authorization), and the MCP steps run as the daemon token's sessionless agent (no Mcp-Session-Id). The agent-token path (minting, the cxa_ bearer on /mcp, its per-initialize session, revocation) is then covered only by the first deploy's smoke, by --session, and by e2e-hosted.mjs on a local Worker. Options: keep the skip (today's behaviour); or add a narrow owner-token route that mints and revokes an agent token for the owner, with tests and contract text, so every release smoke covers it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":286},"end":{"line":291},"content_hash":"a7ad150b792fea0e1d05a24eca45ee15f11a8490f657cd5454870de1f80f6f19"},"summary":"On every deploy after the first the smoke acts with the owner token, so it never mints an agent token or opens an agent token's MCP session","tags":["deploy","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T17:06:35.383014Z","id":"c190906e5b7f2a3eaa221fd54bc5f460361479b68b016344e57bb4de464637e8","body":{"detail":"partialTriggerUpdate (crates/clax-worker/deploy-lib.mjs) is tested on fixture strings built around the line wrangler printed, 'Trigger configuration for \"clax\" was only partially updated' (Cloudflare API code 10013 on the custom-domains call); the rest of that output was not captured, so a wording change in wrangler would make the deploy fail as before rather than retry. waitHealthy now waits until /healthz reports the CLAX_BUILD var of this upload; the local Worker reports it (node smoke-remote.mjs --local shows build smoke-local-<run> and the commit), but no real custom domain has answered with it yet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":547},"end":{"line":561},"content_hash":"c52f4f4af4aabc9f0f21d053bcad373055a7b16159834bdc23daa5cf2deb482d"},"summary":"The partial-trigger retry and the build-matching health wait have not run against the real account","tags":["deploy","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T17:06:35.383053Z","id":"a2d881e80dc714c22efd5ee9efa931d9187bb3a73f27ff3b6fe1efea92dbf470","body":{"detail":"buildId takes sourceCommit() (git rev-parse HEAD) at deploy time, but --no-build uploads build/index_bg.wasm from an earlier build. The ID stays unique per upload, so the health wait is right; the /healthz commit field (CLAX_BUILD_COMMIT stamped at build time, src/instance.rs BUILD_COMMIT) is the one that names the binary's commit.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":455},"end":{"line":456},"content_hash":"dc9d43ddf3868cb2aa523db60d83ae38ef16a1bd1f7d011ef6c2def689a6e31c"},"summary":"With --no-build the build ID's commit prefix is the checked-out HEAD, which may not be the commit the uploaded Worker was built from","tags":["deploy","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:16:42.606475Z","id":"5bf498465e85873b5d699d64bda22809932fa5719017cc0f82254d7fa4385a45","body":{"detail":"checkSiteHost counts any answer below 500 as the zone, the proxied * record, the certificate and the route *.<site>/* at work, assuming Cloudflare answers an unrouted proxied host with 52x or 530 and that the Worker (crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs, once it serves site hosts) answers /_clax/healthz on a host naming no artifact with a status below 500. zoneFound, wildcardFound and certificateFound ran only against public hosts (cloudflare.com NS, www.cloudflare.com's addresses and certificate, a domain that does not resolve); the manual-step printout has not been seen on a deploy whose wildcard record or certificate is missing. The first deploy with --site-domain shows both.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":498},"end":{"line":518},"content_hash":"ce5f9b75d7d1cbbf3e7b5769fafdb0c50a3d655e068ad83e84ea50803c5fa91c"},"summary":"The site host check after a deploy has not run against a real Cloudflare account: what a Worker and the edge answer a random <ID>.<site domain>/_clax/healthz is assumed","tags":["deploy","unverified","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/smoke-remote.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:16:42.606562Z","id":"3f70c4ddb76faba5f87d5af5edd2b05ee9c18a3703db2698d96b531e8a733212","body":{"detail":"The steps from 'site host: health' to 'site: two db artifacts kept apart' assume the routes and shapes the site-origins plan (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-22-clax-run-site-origins.md, Tasks 3, 7, 8 and 11) gives: GET /site-signin 302 to <site>/_clax/session?code=, a site cookie named (__Host-)clax_site, POST /api/artifacts/<ID>/site-code answering {src}, a signed-out /_clax/api/whoami answering 401, PATCH /api/artifacts/<ID> taking site_access, and /_clax/api/docs/<path> answering {doc: {data}}. Until the Worker serves site hosts the health step skips on 404 and the rest skip with it. node --check passes; node smoke-remote.mjs --local has not run against a Worker with SITE_DOMAIN=localhost.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":420},"end":{"line":528},"content_hash":"b31026dff5bce5640009a0c441e68e628199c997eb52c67dce7696bf0b1af3b6"},"summary":"The smoke's site steps have not run: they need a Worker serving site hosts, and --local needs the wasm build","tags":["smoke","unverified","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
